  "mechanism": {
    "before": "On an initialized storage-only Queue, signed info and peek pass stable-leadership guards but advance the real RF3 committed index from 4 to 6. The unchanged regression fails at its intended work oracle.",
    "after": "The byte-identical regression passes with index 4 to 4 in both image modes. Pause and resume remain mutations; subsequent info observes pause without appending another mutation.",
    "read_execution": "The existing operator route authorizes the target before selecting its exact registered query contract. The ordinary pinned resource reader supplies fresh quorum authority. The broker and query share the same metrics/peek SQL and response shaping through read-only framework storage.",
    "archive_floor": "The dispatcher applies the existing S3 query settlement and current-proof check to the exact Queue observation contract when the trusted namespace minimum is S3. Stale consistency refuses before decoding. A read or archive failure never selects a mutation retry or Fleet execution.",
    "initialization": "No local history uses the existing authorized command before attempting any mutation. A selected image with missing Queue tables/statistics emits an internal null sentinel and re-enters that same command with the original admission, arguments and deadline. Other responses/errors refuse rather than authorizing fallback.",
    "boundaries": "Both image modes require signed read success without appends, unsigned/tampered/name-scope refusals, invalid peek-limit refusals, exact stale-consistency refusal, a committed S3 pause behind real denied archive writes, continued Quorum read service, S3 info/peek refusals until archive coverage returns, observation of paused state afterward, and read refusal after losing two Raft hosts."
  },
